TOKEN tinybird_ingest APPEND
TOKEN tinybird_read READ

DESCRIPTION >
Production D1 calls from Gen and Enter, summed per second, route and query,
kept 3 days, to attribute D1 stalls to what ran in the seconds before them.
Each Worker isolate sends its own sums, so one second can have several rows
for the same route and query: always aggregate. `timestamp` is the second the
calls started in, `query_id` names the statement in `d1_query`, and
`error_code` is empty for successful calls.

SCHEMA >
`timestamp`    DateTime               `json:$.timestamp`,
`service`      LowCardinality(String) `json:$.service`,
`environment`  LowCardinality(String) `json:$.environment` DEFAULT 'undefined',
`route_path`   LowCardinality(String) `json:$.route_path` DEFAULT '',
`method`       LowCardinality(String) `json:$.method` DEFAULT '',
`query_id`     LowCardinality(String) `json:$.query_id`,
`error_code`   LowCardinality(String) `json:$.error_code` DEFAULT '',
`calls`        UInt32                 `json:$.calls`,
`total_ms`     UInt32                 `json:$.total_ms`,
`max_ms`       UInt32                 `json:$.max_ms`,
`sql_ms`       Float32                `json:$.sql_ms`,
`rows_read`    UInt64                 `json:$.rows_read`,
`rows_written` UInt64                 `json:$.rows_written`

ENGINE "MergeTree"
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY "toDate(timestamp)"
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY "environment, timestamp"
ENGINE_TTL "timestamp + toIntervalDay(3)"
